            {
                "entry_id": "9f7a4577-b7de-3cf3-8b1a-67bedea84161",
                "word": "Nemrod",
                "pos": "name",
                "lang_code": "fr",
                "forms": [
                    {
                        "form_id": "2f5d20e4-d2e8-4368-a735-bdfce0a1caef",
                        "entry_id": "9f7a4577-b7de-3cf3-8b1a-67bedea84161",
                        "tags": [],
                        "form": "Nimrod"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "db6e7e1e-af9e-336d-b4a9-280cd014b4a5",
                        "entry_id": "9f7a4577-b7de-3cf3-8b1a-67bedea84161",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Petit-fils de Ham, roi de Shinar et chasseur passionné."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "Biblical"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "6c0c2877-46ca-42db-8849-b757e0ea54dd",
                                "sense_id": "db6e7e1e-af9e-336d-b4a9-280cd014b4a5",
                                "text": "Le bedeau nous fit voir aussi une énorme défense d’ivoire suspendue au milieu d’une coupole par des chaînes de fer, et qui semblait la trompe de chasse de quelque géant sarrasin, de quelque Nemrod d’un monde disparu."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "595d85c5-d075-4a4b-ac29-3d1f2cb9fb8d",
                        "source_entry_id": "9f7a4577-b7de-3cf3-8b1a-67bedea84161",
                        "source_sense_id": "db6e7e1e-af9e-336d-b4a9-280cd014b4a5",
                        "target_lang_word": "Nimrod",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "Nimrod",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "58da236f-f73d-3cfc-8db7-6bea58072813",
                                        "entry_id": "3d856fd4-368d-396e-ae4a-b6f40a62a441",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A grandson of Ham; a mighty hunter and king of Shinar."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "35c95da1-d401-4eb7-bf87-ee985c495295",
                                                "sense_id": "58da236f-f73d-3cfc-8db7-6bea58072813",
                                                "text": "Blake's depiction of the biblical Nimrod, whom Erdman traces to Young's poem, recalls Milton's Paradise Lost."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "06368795-646e-41be-9b67-b736c9c829b8",
                                                "sense_id": "58da236f-f73d-3cfc-8db7-6bea58072813",
                                                "text": "In the fourth century St. Ephraim the Syrian wrote, in his commentary on Genesis, that Nimrod 'ruled in Erekh which is Orhay (Edessa)'.[…]In Jewish and thereafter in Moslem tradition, Nimrod was the foe of Abraham."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "7382e1e4-cd0a-4f6f-988f-dde50d3ca2f0",
                                                "sense_id": "58da236f-f73d-3cfc-8db7-6bea58072813",
                                                "text": "The historical facts testify that they were highly developed; Nimrod, a descendant of Ham, therefore making him Hamitic, was the first human king not just of Bible record, but secular history also speaks of him. He ruled over a kingdom that included several cities in Mesopotamia."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "7c7e8d0e-5849-3e10-a249-d5a9854aec28",
                                        "entry_id": "3d856fd4-368d-396e-ae4a-b6f40a62a441",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A British biplane fighter aircraft manufactured by Hawker Aircraft in the early 1930s."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "eff7d104-f707-36cb-b082-61714b0ee4d7",
                                        "entry_id": "3d856fd4-368d-396e-ae4a-b6f40a62a441",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A British maritime patrol aircraft manufactured by Hawker Siddeley, in use from 1969 until 2011."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": []
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "Nimrod",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "bbc9f538-2695-34fa-bc6f-e604a1f76558",
                                        "entry_id": "b52643b6-a9ef-31af-ac82-91797feb00d0",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Any great hunter."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "74ee9053-ad91-4de7-8a10-28148b63bcbb",
                                                "sense_id": "bbc9f538-2695-34fa-bc6f-e604a1f76558",
                                                "text": "Old Ekdal, whom Gregers remembers as Lieutenant Ekdal, his father's partner in the timber business up north and a mighty Nimrod, has, after a term of imprisonment for illicit tree-felling, become a shambling old drunkard, who solaces himself by sporting expeditions in the lean-to attic which his son and he have fitted up for the purpose with withered Christmas trees and a little menagerie of hens, rabbits and the like."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "d427778c-3635-3022-89fa-aabb0fdeff49",
                                        "entry_id": "b52643b6-a9ef-31af-ac82-91797feb00d0",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Alternative letter-case form of nimrod (“fool; idiot”)."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "alt-of"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "word_linkages": []
            },
            {
                "entry_id": "e04fdf0f-b035-3cc1-968b-fc4a3e13a28f",
                "word": "nemrod",
                "pos": "noun",
                "lang_code": "fr",
                "forms": [
                    {
                        "form_id": "c45ebd1d-e52b-489d-9926-f7f192afa557",
                        "entry_id": "e04fdf0f-b035-3cc1-968b-fc4a3e13a28f",
                        "tags": [
                            "plural"
                        ],
                        "form": "nemrods"
                    },
                    {
                        "form_id": "4d08f074-fdc9-456f-98ca-5754c68bba63",
                        "entry_id": "e04fdf0f-b035-3cc1-968b-fc4a3e13a28f",
                        "tags": [],
                        "form": "Nemrod"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "04d557d8-ad98-3fe0-9c53-2bdd35a355a7",
                        "entry_id": "e04fdf0f-b035-3cc1-968b-fc4a3e13a28f",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Chasseur passionné qui tue beaucoup de gibier."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "9b0fce16-d450-49af-ad3e-97d5fa45cb02",
                                "sense_id": "04d557d8-ad98-3fe0-9c53-2bdd35a355a7",
                                "text": "Il résolut donc d’aller battre pendant quelques heures les broussailles et les taillis des alentours. Lions, hyènes ou léopardés n’étaient pas pour embarrasser un Nemrod tel que lui, des forêts africaines."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "3d4b9c5d-f07d-4b55-b328-9a8f72cd7809",
                                "sense_id": "04d557d8-ad98-3fe0-9c53-2bdd35a355a7",
                                "text": "[…] c’était chez lui que j’avais fait, en tuant un lièvre, mes débuts dans la science des Nemrod et des Elzéar Blaze."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "1fbdc181-8705-4342-806c-03cf36198357",
                                "sense_id": "04d557d8-ad98-3fe0-9c53-2bdd35a355a7",
                                "text": "Car la région que nous traversons est assez giboyeuse, et les grands nemrods de la m’halla, […], qui ont emmené des meutes de lévriers et des faucons chasseurs, font des hécatombes de lièvres, de perdrix, de poules de Carthage, de renards et de chacals."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "db4b2c7c-9fbf-4c33-ba20-89e06bcd3892",
                                "sense_id": "04d557d8-ad98-3fe0-9c53-2bdd35a355a7",
                                "text": "Dans les jours qui suivirent, il se prépara des choses mystérieuses, ce qui n’empêcha pas la grand-père de me raconter une ou deux de ces aventures incroyables qui arrivent aux grands nemrods."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "ae31387b-3f32-4466-8f68-3594c3ab593b",
                                "sense_id": "04d557d8-ad98-3fe0-9c53-2bdd35a355a7",
                                "text": "Les nemrods, (…), pourront se procurer leur permis au montant de 16.80$ et se diriger vers les zones 4, 5, 6, 7, 8 ou 10 dès samedi prochain."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "a30a694e-d0d5-4ebe-8cc4-972bb06ef23d",
                                "sense_id": "04d557d8-ad98-3fe0-9c53-2bdd35a355a7",
                                "text": "Quelques jours après le retour du huard, Henry vit débarquer les nemrods, équipés d’armes de précision et de longues-vues."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "9950ca1d-92d7-4a98-b779-2f38e0f7dc80",
                        "source_entry_id": "e04fdf0f-b035-3cc1-968b-fc4a3e13a28f",
                        "source_sense_id": "04d557d8-ad98-3fe0-9c53-2bdd35a355a7",
